From 2a9b9dc606b05f41ea98d47a01243ecd82111ded Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: suharvest <suharvest@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 3 Jul 2026 20:59:07 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 27/38] feat(omni-tts): external speaker-embedding conditioning
 path (re-port ba9ecdb)

Re-add the Base speaker-encoder (external-embedding) conditioning path on the
v0.9.0 runtime. speakerName/speakerId only resolve to preset codec token IDs
and cannot carry an arbitrary voice-clone vector, so:

- TalkerGenerationRequest gains an optional std::vector<float> speakerEmbedding
  (length = talkerHiddenSize, FP32; precomputed offline / by a speaker encoder).
- projectToTalkerInput converts it to FP16, uploads into a dedicated
  mSpeakerEmbeddingBuffer, and routes it to the preamble kernel; a size
  mismatch is rejected with LOG_ERROR.
- talkerMLPKernels: assistantPreambleKernel/invokeAssistantPreamble gain
  trailing speakerEmbeddingPtr/hasSpeakerEmbedding (defaulted, so existing
  callers are unaffected). When present, the speaker row (row 6 in the 8-row
  layout, row 7 in the 9-row language layout) IS the external embedding (no
  ttsPad add), overriding the named-speaker token path.

Opt-in: empty embedding (default) = upstream named-speaker token path,
byte-identical behavior.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01MHEXK41deYx6375K4q3MQb

